My ex-girlfriend kind of like weirdly didn't get it.
我的前女友不知为何就是无法理解。

1295
00:45:25.230 --> 00:45:27.870
And I always was like, wait a minute, this is problematic.
我当时总觉得，等一下，这有点问题。

1296
00:45:27.870 --> 00:45:32.030
Like I love this thing so much and she didn't get it.
我这么喜欢这东西，而她却不理解。

1297
00:45:32.030 --> 00:45:35.790
And then I, one of the first things I did when I was getting to know Jordana,
然后我，在开始了解若尔达娜时做的第一件事之一，

1298
00:45:35.790 --> 00:45:40.190
I sent her this thing and she wept and she called me, you know what I mean?
就是把这东西发给了她，她居然哭了，然后打电话给我，你懂我的意思吗？

1299
00:45:40.190 --> 00:45:43.630
Like she really like affected her in the way that it affected me.
就像它对她的触动和我对她的触动一样。

1300
00:45:44.190 --> 00:45:47.710
And I felt so good that she responded that way.
她有这样的反应，让我觉得感觉太棒了。

1301
00:45:48.270 --> 00:45:51.070
But at the same time, she loves some things I don't love.
但与此同时，她喜欢的一些东西我并不喜欢。

1302
00:45:51.070 --> 00:45:52.830
And I love some things she doesn't love.
而我也喜欢一些她不喜欢的东西。

1303
00:45:52.830 --> 00:45:54.670
And that's also something you have to live with.
这也是你必须接受并与之相处的一部分。

1304
00:45:54.670 --> 00:45:57.870
That you're not always going to have the same response to something.
那就是你们对某件事的反应并不总是一致的。

1305
00:45:59.070 --> 00:45:59.870
Absolutely, right?
完全是这样，对吧？

1306
00:45:59.870 --> 00:46:00.830
And that's okay.
而且没关系。

1307
00:46:00.830 --> 00:46:03.150
And you have to exist in that discomfort because you're two different people.
你必须在这种不适感中相处，因为你们是两个不同的人。

1308
00:46:03.150 --> 00:46:05.630
But don't you want to have enough key overlaps?
但难道你不想拥有足够多的关键共同点吗？

1309
00:46:05.630 --> 00:46:07.630
You wanted Jordana to like that thing.
你当时希望乔丹娜也喜欢那个东西。

1310
00:46:07.630 --> 00:46:08.990
And now I need to know what that thing is.
现在我很想知道那个东西到底是什么。

1311
00:46:08.990 --> 00:46:10.350
You can tell me offline maybe.
也许你可以私下告诉我。

1312
00:46:10.350 --> 00:46:10.670
Yeah.
对。

1313
00:46:12.110 --> 00:46:18.030
I know a woman who got divorced is actually a friend of one of my sisters.
我认识一个离过婚的女人，其实是我其中一个姐妹的朋友。

1314
00:46:18.030 --> 00:46:18.990
She got divorced.
她离婚了。

1315
00:46:19.710 --> 00:46:24.190
And she said, me and my husband loved all the same movies,
她说，我和我丈夫喜欢所有相同的电影，

1316
00:46:24.190 --> 00:46:26.510
all the same TV shows and all the same music.
所有相同的电视剧和所有相同的音乐。

1317
00:46:26.510 --> 00:46:27.870
And I thought that was enough.
而我以为这就足够了。

1318
00:46:28.990 --> 00:46:31.390
Like that was the thing that kind of made her feel like,
就好像这让她有一种感觉，

1319
00:46:31.390 --> 00:46:34.030
oh my god, we're kindred spirits.
天哪，我们真是志同道合。

1320
00:46:34.030 --> 00:46:35.310
But it can't only be that.
但不能仅仅只有这些。

1321
00:46:35.310 --> 00:46:41.470
Although you do end up exploring a lot of entertainment options with your partner.
尽管你确实最终会和伴侣一起探索很多娱乐选择。

1322
00:46:41.470 --> 00:46:45.150
Like it's nice to be able to like agree on a movie or agree on a TV show.
比如能对一部电影或一部电视剧达成一致，感觉很好。

1323
00:46:45.150 --> 00:46:47.950
Can I bring it all full circle as we start season four?
在我们开始第四季的时候，我能把这一切串联起来吗？

1324
00:46:47.950 --> 00:46:49.950
And we started off with a clip from our first,
我们一开始播放了一段我们第一季的剪辑，

1325
00:46:51.150 --> 00:46:54.990
I liked how Alex started this episode out with a clip of our very first episode
我喜欢亚历克斯用我们第一集的一段剪辑来开启这一集的方式

1326
00:46:54.990 --> 00:46:56.510
of this whole podcaSt.
整个播客的核心。

1327
00:46:56.510 --> 00:46:59.790
Because here's what I thought about when we started this podcaSt.
因为当我开始做这个播客时，我想到了这一点。

1328
00:46:59.790 --> 00:47:01.870
I thought about the Star Wars teSt.
我想到了《星球大战》测试。

1329
00:47:01.870 --> 00:47:06.430
I thought about Ted sitting on a couch looking at Stella wondering if she's going to like Star Wars.
我想到了特德坐在沙发上看着斯特拉，心里琢磨她会不会喜欢《星球大战》。

1330
00:47:06.430 --> 00:47:10.190
Because you were going to watch How I Met Your Mother with your wife,
因为你打算和你的妻子一起看《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

1331
00:47:10.190 --> 00:47:14.190
who you married before she ever saw one episode of How I Met Your Mother.
你在她看过任何一集《老爸老妈浪漫史》之前就娶了她。

1332
00:47:14.190 --> 00:47:18.830
So the second you pitched the idea of us doing this podcast to me and to Alec.
所以当你向我和亚历克提出我们一起做这个播客的想法时。

1333
00:47:18.830 --> 00:47:20.750
And you said it was kind of Jordana's idea too.
而且你说这也算是乔丹娜的想法。

1334
00:47:20.750 --> 00:47:25.470
I mean, it came from your guys' discussion of that she had never seen this 10 year body of work you did.
我的意思是，这源于你们俩的讨论，因为她从来没看过你花了10年心血完成的作品。

1335
00:47:25.470 --> 00:47:30.270
The very first thing I thought about was this episode of How I Met Your Mother.
我脑子里想到的第一件事就是《老爸老妈浪漫史》的这一集。

1336
00:47:30.270 --> 00:47:32.510
Was Sarah Chock on the couch?
莎拉·乔克当时在沙发上吗？

1337
00:47:32.510 --> 00:47:34.030
What's she going to think of this thing?
她会对这东西有什么看法？

1338
00:47:34.030 --> 00:47:38.670
And I felt nervous knowing Jordana, your wife was going to watch How I Met Your Mother.
一想到你的妻子乔丹娜要看《老爸老妈浪漫史》，我就感到紧张。

1339
00:47:38.670 --> 00:47:41.470
And I was like, I really hope she likes this TV show.
当时我在想，我真的很希望她喜欢这部电视剧。

1340
00:47:42.350 --> 00:47:43.870
What is what is this whole thing going to be?
这整件事到底会变成什么样？

1341
00:47:43.870 --> 00:47:44.990
Another spoiler alert.
另一个剧透预警。

1342
00:47:44.990 --> 00:47:46.990
She really likes this TV show.
她真的很喜欢这部电视剧。

1343
00:47:46.990 --> 00:47:49.070
It's the deep relief and joy.
那是深深的释怀与喜悦。

1344
00:47:49.070 --> 00:47:50.670
That's the wait for it.
这就是所谓的“拭目以待”。

1345
00:47:50.670 --> 00:47:51.550
Lightful.
太美妙了。

1346
00:47:59.390 --> 00:48:05.230
And now we're up to one of our favorite segments of the show that we call the C-Blah.
现在我们迎来了节目中最喜爱的环节之一，我们称之为 C-Blah。

1347
00:48:05.230 --> 00:48:08.990
C-Blah, C-Blah, C-Blah, C-Blah.
C-Blah, C-Blah, C-Blah, C-Blah。

1348
00:48:08.990 --> 00:48:11.310
No, no, we don't know one, not one of us.
不，不，我们都不知道，没有一个人知道。

1349
00:48:11.310 --> 00:48:12.590
We don't know how it started.
我们不知道它是怎么开始的。

1350
00:48:12.590 --> 00:48:13.222
We don't know.
我们都不知道。

1351
00:48:13.222 --> 00:48:14.350
There's no meaning to it.
这没什么意义。

1352
00:48:14.350 --> 00:48:15.070
Yeah.
对。

1353
00:48:15.070 --> 00:48:15.550
It's okay.
还行。

1354
00:48:15.550 --> 00:48:16.030
I like it.
我挺喜欢的。

1355
00:48:16.030 --> 00:48:16.750
It feels right.
感觉对了。

1356
00:48:16.750 --> 00:48:17.790
It just feels right.
就是感觉对了。

1357
00:48:17.790 --> 00:48:21.870
I have a wonderful letter to read for us from Elle.
我这有一封艾尔写给我们的精彩信件要读。

1358
00:48:23.070 --> 00:48:26.350
Dear Josh, Craig, and Alec, isn't it nice when they include you, Alec?
“亲爱的乔希、克雷格和亚历克，他们把你也算上了，挺不错的吧，亚历克？”

1359
00:48:26.350 --> 00:48:27.870
I'm at least someone does.
至少还有人记得我。

1360
00:48:29.950 --> 00:48:31.310
Hi, my name is Elle.
“嗨，我叫艾尔。”

1361
00:48:31.310 --> 00:48:35.310
And Himyim has been a huge part of my life for around eight years now.
“大约八年来，《老爸老妈浪漫史》一直是我生活中非常重要的一部分。”

1362
00:48:35.870 --> 00:48:40.110
Firstly, I'd just like to say thank you so much for starting
“首先，我只想对你们发起”

1363
00:48:40.110 --> 00:48:42.110
Himyim, how we made Your Mother.
“《老爸老妈浪漫史》播客表达由衷的感谢。”

1364
00:48:42.110 --> 00:48:45.710
To hear your perspectives and reflections on this amazing piece of art you all brought to life
“听到你们对这部由大家共同赋予生命的伟大艺术作品的观点和反思，”

1365
00:48:45.710 --> 00:48:48.190
has really revived the magic of the show.
“真的让我重新感受到了这部剧的魅力。”

1366
00:48:48.190 --> 00:48:52.190
I was first introduced to Himyim in 2018 by an ex-boyfriend.
“我是在2018年通过前男友第一次接触到《老爸老妈浪漫史》的。”

1367
00:48:52.190 --> 00:48:53.870
I'd heard of the show, but never seen it.
“我听说过这部剧，但从未看过。”

1368
00:48:54.430 --> 00:48:56.270
I became hooked instantly.
“我瞬间就迷上了。”

1369
00:48:56.270 --> 00:49:01.470
I saw myself in Ted and his longing for the one in Robin and her ambition,
“我在泰德身上看到了自己对真爱执着的渴望，在罗宾身上看到了她的野心，”

1370
00:49:01.470 --> 00:49:05.550
in Lily and her softness, and in Marshall and his love for food.
“在莉莉身上看到了她的温柔，在马歇尔身上看到了他对美食的热爱。”

1371
00:49:05.550 --> 00:49:09.710
Despite the feminist I am, rightly or wrongly, I've always loved Barney too.
“尽管我是一个女权主义者，不管对错，我也一直很喜欢巴尼。”

1372
00:49:10.510 --> 00:49:14.030
After my ex and I broke up, I struggled to watch the show again because memories of
“我和前男友分手后，我很难再看这部剧，因为”

1373
00:49:14.030 --> 00:49:15.870
watching it with my ex made it too painful.
“和前男友一起看的记忆让这一切变得太痛苦了。”

1374
00:49:16.750 --> 00:49:20.110
However, a few months after we broke up, I gave it a go.
“然而，在我们分手几个月后，我决定再试一次。”

1375
00:49:20.110 --> 00:49:23.150
And it was like watching the show through a completely new lens.
“那种感觉就像是通过一副全新的有色眼镜在看这部剧。”

1376
00:49:23.710 --> 00:49:26.190
Since then, I've suffered a lot with my mental health.
从那以后，我的心理健康状况一直饱受折磨。

1377
00:49:26.190 --> 00:49:28.510
And Himyim has been there for me every time.
而《老爸老妈浪漫史》每一次都陪伴着我度过难关。

1378
00:49:28.510 --> 00:49:33.390
No matter how life changes, I always have my four best friends waiting for me at McLaren's.
无论生活如何变迁，我的四个挚友总是在麦克拉伦酒吧等我。

1379
00:49:34.030 --> 00:49:38.830
Around two years ago, I had a breakthrough when I was finally diagnosed with ADHD.
大约两年前，我终于被确诊患有多动症，病情取得了突破性的进展。

1380
00:49:38.830 --> 00:49:42.510
As silly as this may sound, there's an episode where Barney talks about being told
听起来可能有点傻，但有一集里巴尼说自己被告知

1381
00:49:42.590 --> 00:49:46.030
he has AD something and that really made me feel seen.
他得了“多什么症”，那一幕真的让我觉得自己被理解了。

1382
00:49:46.030 --> 00:49:48.270
If Barney can tackle it, so can I.
既然巴尼能克服它，我也行。

1383
00:49:49.390 --> 00:49:52.590
Thank you from the bottom of my heart for creating something truly magical
发自内心地感谢你们创造了如此真正神奇的作品

1384
00:49:52.590 --> 00:49:56.590
that I can return to time and time again and still learn new lessons from.
让我能够一次又一次地重温，并且依然能从中领悟到新的道理。

1385
00:49:56.590 --> 00:50:00.190
I can happily share that like Ted, my heartbreak didn't laSt.
我很开心地告诉大家，就像特德一样，我的心碎并没有持续下去。

1386
00:50:00.190 --> 00:50:03.630
And I'm currently introducing my partner of three years to Himyim.
我目前正在带我交往三年的伴侣一起看《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

1387
00:50:04.190 --> 00:50:09.150
He's a Robin and Ted lover and we've shared many laughs while eating a sandwich and watching
他是罗宾和特德的粉丝，我们在边吃三明治边看剧的时候

1388
00:50:09.150 --> 00:50:09.790
the show.
一起分享了许多欢笑。

1389
00:50:10.750 --> 00:50:12.990
Thank you all for changing my life.
谢谢你们所有人改变了我的生活。

1390
00:50:12.990 --> 00:50:17.550
I'd be a major mess, major mess without this show.
如果没有这部剧，我会彻底崩溃的，彻底崩溃。

1391
00:50:17.550 --> 00:50:22.670
P.S., you've even inspired my dissertation for which I'm currently writing a screenplay.
顺便说一句，你们甚至启发了我的毕业论文，我目前正在为它写一个剧本。

1392
00:50:22.670 --> 00:50:23.950
Love and light, Elle.
带着爱与光，艾尔。

1393
00:50:23.950 --> 00:50:25.390
Fantastic.
太棒了。

1394
00:50:25.390 --> 00:50:26.430
Thanks, Elle.
谢谢你，艾尔。

1395
00:50:26.430 --> 00:50:29.390
We're so happy to be on this journey with you.
我们很高兴能陪伴你走过这段旅程。

1396
00:50:30.990 --> 00:50:31.790
It's so fitting.
真是太巧了。

1397
00:50:31.790 --> 00:50:34.990
You just were talking about how so many women relate to Ted, right?
你刚才还在说有多少女性对特德感同身受，对吧？

1398
00:50:34.990 --> 00:50:35.550
Yeah.
是的。

1399
00:50:35.550 --> 00:50:39.950
And this is like right on cue, like someone like she's saying, I feel like I'm Ted.
这就好像是提前排练好的一样，就像有人在说，我觉得自己就是特德。

1400
00:50:39.950 --> 00:50:41.470
And then I love her connection to Barney.
而且我特别喜欢她和巴尼的这种共鸣。

1401
00:50:41.470 --> 00:50:45.150
She's saying Barney can be problematic, but he also admits he has these moments
她说巴尼可能会有些问题，但他也承认自己有这些时刻

1402
00:50:45.150 --> 00:50:48.990
of admitting vulnerability and even that one little acknowledgement of IAVD, something
会展露脆弱，甚至还有那一点点对 IAVD 的认可，有些东西

1403
00:50:49.550 --> 00:50:52.670
that really, that stock, there's something cool about that.
真的，那种存货，那种感觉真的很酷。

1404
00:50:52.670 --> 00:50:56.590
Those moments Barney, you get a glimpse of what's going on for Barney
在那些时刻，巴尼，你能一窥巴尼内心深处的想法

1405
00:50:57.630 --> 00:50:58.990
and see that humanity a little bit.
并稍微看到那种人性的一面。

1406
00:50:58.990 --> 00:51:00.910
Like that's a very quick moment.
就像那是一个非常短暂的瞬间。

1407
00:51:00.910 --> 00:51:02.270
I love that moment.
我喜欢那个时刻。

1408
00:51:02.830 --> 00:51:04.190
Stayed with you, Elle.
它一直留在你心中，艾尔。

1409
00:51:04.190 --> 00:51:06.430
It's a real tight rope walk what you guys were doing with Barney.
你们对巴尼的处理真的是在走钢丝。

1410
00:51:06.430 --> 00:51:12.190
I mean, you always pulled him back from going over the like odious cliff.
我的意思是，你们总能把他从跌落到令人厌恶的悬崖边缘拉回来。

1411
00:51:12.190 --> 00:51:12.830
Yes.
没错。

1412
00:51:12.830 --> 00:51:15.950
You know, there was something about, you could almost get too faSt.
你知道的，某种程度上，你甚至差点就做得太过了。

1413
00:51:15.950 --> 00:51:20.510
I imagine you could intuitively sense when it was time for Barney to get his come up and
我猜你们能凭直觉感知到什么时候该让巴尼尝尝苦果

1414
00:51:20.510 --> 00:51:24.110
when it was time to pull the rug out from under him, when it was time to reveal
什么时候该揭穿他，什么时候该展现

1415
00:51:24.110 --> 00:51:27.150
that he was dealing with a lot of pain and insecurity.
他其实在承受着许多痛苦和不安。

1416
00:51:28.430 --> 00:51:28.830
Yeah.
是的。

1417
00:51:28.830 --> 00:51:31.550
And then when he had to be Barney again, like he did at the end of this episode.
然后当他必须再次做回巴尼时，就像这集结尾那样。

1418
00:51:31.550 --> 00:51:34.510
But even at the end of this episode, we just talked about like, you know,
但即使在这集的结尾，我们刚刚也聊过，你知道的，

1419
00:51:34.510 --> 00:51:38.190
that little moment when he turns on that TV, he knows exactly what time it is.
当他打开电视的那一小会儿，他清楚地知道现在几点了。

1420
00:51:38.190 --> 00:51:41.470
He knows Robin's going to be on New York one and he just wanted to see your face again.
他知道罗宾会出现在纽约一台上，他只是想再看一眼你的脸。

1421
00:51:41.470 --> 00:51:41.790
Yeah.
是的。

1422
00:51:41.790 --> 00:51:44.750
Before he goes back into the room and to find his own nightstand,
在他走回房间去寻找他自己的床头柜之前，

1423
00:51:44.750 --> 00:51:46.910
you know that he's in love with her.
你知道他爱上了她。

1424
00:51:46.910 --> 00:51:48.510
This is going way back.
这要追溯到很久以前了。

1425
00:51:48.510 --> 00:51:56.190
But the gang even understands after a while how much Barney needs his costume.
但过了一段时间，大家甚至都能理解巴尼有多么需要他的伪装。

1426
00:51:56.830 --> 00:51:57.390
Yeah.
是的。

1427
00:51:57.390 --> 00:52:00.910
And one of the best examples of that, and again, I think this might even be first season,
而其中最好的例子之一，再说一次，我觉得这可能甚至是第一季的，

1428
00:52:00.910 --> 00:52:04.830
